  "id": "COMPOUND:1178 - PROTEIN:898",
  "verbalization": "Zopiclone is likely to interact with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit alpha-4 through a shared target relationship with other GABA receptor subunits. The evidence suggests that zopiclone targets the alpha-1 subunit, which in turn is targeted by ganaxolone and meprobamate, both of which also target alpha-4. This implies a potential mechanism where zopiclone may act on the same receptor subunit as these other drugs, possibly through a common pathway or a shared functional role. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship across different targets, suggesting that the interaction between zopiclone and alpha-4 is well-supported by the available data. The recurring involvement of alpha-1 and alpha-4 in multiple target relationships highlights the importance of GABA receptor subunit alpha in the pharmacological effects of these compounds.",
